arm64: add ioremap_cache_ns() shim for NXP SDK callers

drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/{bman,qman}_driver.c calls ioremap_cache_ns()
to map the QBMan portal cache-enabled region.  NXP's lf-6.x kernels
ship this helper in arch/arm64/include/asm/io.h as

  #define ioremap_cache_ns(addr, size) \
        ioremap_prot((addr), (size), PROT_NORMAL_NS)

but PROT_NORMAL_NS (TLB attr Non-Secure) is an NXP-private addition
absent from mainline.  On stock linux-6.6.137 the call is therefore
an implicit-function-declaration and dies under -Werror:

  drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/bman_driver.c:194:42:
    error: implicit declaration of function 'ioremap_cache_ns';
           did you mean 'ioremap_cache'?
  drivers/staging/fsl_qbman/qman_driver.c:451:42: <same>

Provide a one-line shim that aliases ioremap_cache_ns() to the existing
mainline ioremap_cache().  The two attribute sets differ only in the
NS (Non-Secure) bit; on this SoC running in EL2 we never enter the
secure world via these portals, so the cacheable mapping is functionally
correct (and is what the older 5.4 SDK overlay used before NXP added
the dedicated _ns variant).

Placing the shim after the existing "#define ioremap_cache ioremap_cache"
self-define keeps it in the same idiom and just before the static-inline
ioremap_cache() definition that backs both names.

--- a/arch/arm64/include/asm/io.h
+++ b/arch/arm64/include/asm/io.h
@@ -162,6 +162,10 @@
 #include <asm-generic/io.h>
 
 #define ioremap_cache ioremap_cache
+/* NXP SDK compat: lf-6.x defines this with PROT_NORMAL_NS; mainline lacks it.
+ * Cacheable mapping is a strict superset for our portal-CE use; alias it. */
+#define ioremap_cache_ns(addr, size) ioremap_cache((addr), (size))
+
 static inline void __iomem *ioremap_cache(phys_addr_t addr, size_t size)
 {
 	if (pfn_is_map_memory(__phys_to_pfn(addr)))
